{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"map-multimap","title":"map & multimap","group":"STL Containers & Iterators","order":52,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>std::map&lt;K, V&gt;</code> stores key → value pairs sorted by key, with unique keys and O(log n) operations. <code>std::multimap</code> allows repeated keys.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>Core operations</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;map&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::map&lt;std::string, int&gt; stock{{\"apple\", 5}, {\"pear\", 2}};\n    stock[\"kiwi\"] = 7;                          // insert or overwrite\n    stock[\"apple\"] += 1;\n    stock.insert({\"pear\", 100});                // no effect: key exists\n    stock.emplace(\"fig\", 3);\n\n    for (const auto&amp; [fruit, qty] : stock) std::cout &lt;&lt; fruit &lt;&lt; '=' &lt;&lt; qty &lt;&lt; ' ';   // sorted by key\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    if (auto it = stock.find(\"kiwi\"); it != stock.end()) std::cout &lt;&lt; \"kiwi: \" &lt;&lt; it-&gt;second &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; stock.count(\"mango\") &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; stock.contains(\"fig\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    stock.erase(\"pear\");\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; stock.size() &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; stock.at(\"fig\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>apple=6 fig=3 kiwi=7 pear=2\nkiwi: 7\n0 1\n3 3</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>The <code>operator[]</code> trap</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;map&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\nint main() {\n    std::map&lt;std::string, int&gt; ages{{\"ada\", 36}};\n    if (ages[\"bob\"] == 0) std::cout &lt;&lt; \"bob not found?\\n\";   // [] INSERTS \"bob\" with 0!\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; ages.size() &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    // const std::map&lt;...&gt;&amp; cref = ages; cref[\"x\"];          // error: no const operator[]\n    try { std::cout &lt;&lt; ages.at(\"cy\"); } catch (const std::out_of_range&amp;) { std::cout &lt;&lt; \"at() throws\\n\"; }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>bob not found?\n2\nat() throws</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Access</th><th>Missing key</th><th>Use for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>m[key]</code></td><td>Inserts a default-constructed value</td><td>Counting, building up (<code>freq[word]++</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>m.at(key)</code></td><td>Throws <code>std::out_of_range</code></td><td>Must exist</td></tr><tr><td><code>m.find(key)</code></td><td>Returns <code>m.end()</code></td><td>Lookup without side effects</td></tr><tr><td><code>m.contains(key)</code> (C++20) / <code>m.count(key)</code></td><td><code>false</code> / <code>0</code></td><td>Existence check</td></tr><tr><td><code>m.insert_or_assign(k, v)</code> / <code>m.try_emplace(k, args…)</code></td><td>Inserts</td><td>Explicit upsert / insert-if-absent</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-chart-bar\"></i>Word frequency &amp; range queries</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;map&gt;\n#include &lt;sstream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::istringstream text(\"the cat and the hat and the bat\");\n    std::map&lt;std::string, int&gt; freq;\n    std::string w;\n    while (text &gt;&gt; w) ++freq[w];\n    for (const auto&amp; [word, n] : freq) std::cout &lt;&lt; word &lt;&lt; ':' &lt;&lt; n &lt;&lt; ' ';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::map&lt;int, std::string&gt; events{{900, \"standup\"}, {1200, \"lunch\"}, {1500, \"review\"}, {1800, \"gym\"}};\n    for (auto it = events.lower_bound(1000); it != events.upper_bound(1600); ++it)   // keys in [1000, 1600]\n        std::cout &lt;&lt; it-&gt;first &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; it-&gt;second &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>and:2 bat:1 cat:1 hat:1 the:3\n1200 lunch\n1500 review</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-sitemap\"></i><code>std::multimap</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;map&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\nint main() {\n    std::multimap&lt;std::string, std::string&gt; phone{{\"ada\", \"111\"}, {\"bob\", \"222\"}, {\"ada\", \"333\"}};\n    auto [first, last] = phone.equal_range(\"ada\");     // all entries with key \"ada\"\n    for (auto it = first; it != last; ++it) std::cout &lt;&lt; it-&gt;second &lt;&lt; ' ';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; phone.count(\"ada\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>111 333 2</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>map vs unordered_map?</summary><div><p><code>map</code> is a balanced BST: O(log n) operations, keys iterated in sorted order, supports <code>lower_bound</code>/range queries, needs <code>&lt;</code>. <code>unordered_map</code> is a hash table: O(1) average (O(n) worst) operations, no ordering, needs <code>std::hash</code> and <code>==</code>. Use <code>unordered_map</code> for pure lookup speed, <code>map</code> when order or ranges matter or worst-case guarantees are needed.</p></div></details></section>"}